{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And olive oil, a hin.</b> There is no doubt that this quantity of oil would not have sufficed to mix with the full quantity of those spices. Rather, they boiled the oil together with the spices' boiling water, or they floated it upon the water of their steeping until the water was gone — through boiling or through gentle heat applied within the water — and the oil remained in the manner of perfumers. And on this there was a dispute among our Sages of blessed memory: whether they boiled it together with their boiling water, or floated it upon their steeping water and dissolved them in vapor through gentle heat (Horayot 11a)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:35.986738914Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}